841,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMjM0ODQx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/23234841?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/925236118","html_url":"https://github.com/925236118","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/925236118/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/925236118/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/925236118/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/925236118/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/925236118/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/925236118/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/925236118/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/925236118/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/925236118/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-16T02:01:17Z","updated_at":"2025-09-16T02:01:17Z","body":"Since version 4.3, this default behavior has been modified, which has left me and my friends confused. We once gave up on updates 4.4 and beyond (including the recently released 4.5 version), but now I have found this solution here. Perhaps we can continue to stay updated and learn.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3294575307/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3300940193","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/101306#issuecomment-3300940193","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101306","id":3300940193,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7EwFmh","user":{"login":"revaraver","id":29756950,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI5NzU2OTUw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/29756950?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/revaraver","html_url":"https://github.com/revaraver","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/revaraver/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/revaraver/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/revaraver/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/revaraver/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/revaraver/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/revaraver/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/revaraver/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/revaraver/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/revaraver/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-17T02:12:21Z","updated_at":"2025-09-17T02:12:21Z","body":"This is a change I can't understand. The only use case I can think of is that replace completion is used by programmers to fix spelling errors. And crucially, VSCode's default completion method is insert completion, not replace completion. Changing such a frequently used completion key is completely inexplicable, and this completion strategy is truly baffling. Do programmers spend more time fixing spelling errors than changing function prefixes? For example, if I add @export prefix before var, without adding a space first and then press the left arrow key, it will replace the entire var with @export?","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3300940193/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4091533104","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/101306#issuecomment-4091533104","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101306","id":4091533104,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7z39cw","user":{"login":"EdwardChanCH","id":97891482,"node_id":"U_kgDOBdW0mg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/97891482?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/EdwardChanCH","html_url":"https://github.com/EdwardChanCH","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EdwardChanCH/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EdwardChanCH/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EdwardChanCH/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EdwardChanCH/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EdwardChanCH/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EdwardChanCH/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EdwardChanCH/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EdwardChanCH/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EdwardChanCH/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-19T16:39:26Z","updated_at":"2026-03-19T16:46:48Z","body":"> My question is, when is this the intention of the programmer?\n> When would you start typing in the middle of a word and wanting the whole thing replaced?\n\nOne (very niche) example is when replacing `apply_force()` with `apply_central_force()`, by typing and using auto-complete in the middle of the method name.\n\nIf auto-replacement is disabled by holding `Shift`, it becomes `apply_central_force(force()`.\n\n> You can open the Editor Settings menu, then switch to the Shortcuts tab. Then search for the shortcut, and you can edit it. If you want ui_text_completion_accept to use Enter, make sure to remove it from the ui_text_completion_replace shortcut too.\n\nThis would be fine for solo developers, but not that practical for those who upgrade Godot often, or share computers with others.\n\n> Maybe we can swap the defaults, so Enter/Tab is insert and Shift+Enter/Shift+Tab is replace.\n\nI think this would be the least disruptive change while still achieving the goal.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4091533104/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4111453946","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/101306#issuecomment-4111453946","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101306","id":4111453946,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc71D876","user":{"login":"Ignawesome","id":21315198,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxMzE1MTk4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/21315198?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ignawesome","html_url":"https://github.com/Ignawesome","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ignawesome/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ignawesome/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ignawesome/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ignawesome/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ignawesome/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ignawesome/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ignawesome/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ignawesome/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ignawesome/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-23T15:21:00Z","updated_at":"2026-03-23T15:21:00Z","body":"I've been using Godot for over 3 years and this is the first time I've heard about shift+enter to change the autocomplete behavior. When this was introduced I assumed it was a bug and learned to live with it 😅\n\nI don't have a CS background, and I started using VS code for Godot, but even as someone who looked for all the tips and tricks, editor configs and workflow optimization I could find, I never ran across this workaround until now. I had accepted I needed to add a space before trying to insert an autocompletion.\nThat's my experience anyway.\n\nI think having the opposite behavior (holding shift for replacing) is more intuitive, as I've never needed to replace something like this, I usually just delete what's not needed first. Even if I needed to delete the following word after inserting, just using ctrl+delete solves that instantly. On the other hand, inserting something and replacing something else by mistake takes _several_ inputs to correct.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4111453946/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]